@startuml
title Harness functions — framework user, orchestrator agent, step subagents, host, adapter, harness

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30
skinparam BoxPadding 10

actor "Framework user" as User
participant "Workflow Orchestrator agent" as Orch
participant "Step subagent" as Sub
participant "Host\n(GitHub Copilot runtime:\nCLI / app / VS Code Copilot)" as Host
participant "Adapter\n(github-copilot)" as Adapter
participant "Harness\n(host-agnostic core)" as Harness

note over Harness
  Every completed function invocation appends one
  entry to its session's log — logs/<sessionId>.log.jsonl
  (a workflow instance is a cross-log view, ordered by
  timestamp under the single-driver invariant). Every call/return
  pair below names its contract's actual In/Out fields.
end note

note over Adapter
  Classifies each concrete host hook into a harness
  boundary and invokes the core's ""Command"" surface
  only — no services, no stores, no config of its own
  beyond its own binding (see adapter-src-classes.puml).
end note

== Conversation start ==
User -> Host : engage a facilitator agent (VMO / RTE / SM)\nwith a request — a question or an intent
Host -> Adapter : hook ""userPromptSubmitted"" / ""userPromptTransformed"" — agent-scoped\n(fires only while a framework orchestrator is the active agent)
note right of Adapter
  H0 is agent-scoped (rendered into each orchestrator's
  own .agent.md frontmatter): C7 holds structurally —
  the hook never fires for a non-framework agent, so
  there is no runtime foreign-session branch here.
end note
Adapter -> Harness : ""0 start-session""(agent, sessionId, parentSessionId: null)
Harness --> Adapter : { session: { agent, sessionId, parentSessionId } }
Adapter -> Harness : ""1 resolve-workflow-instructions""(sessionId, parentSessionId: null)
Harness --> Adapter : { instructions: [selection-, step-resolution-,\nno-next-step-, reports-handling refs] }
Adapter -> Harness : ""2 resolve-workflow-skills""(sessionId, parentSessionId: null)
Harness --> Adapter : { skills: [selection skill,\none procedure skill per facilitated workflow] }
Adapter -> Adapter : render the context —\ninline instructions + skill load directives
Adapter --> Host : ""modifiedTransformedPrompt"" =\nhint + context + the prompt
Host --> Orch : session opens carrying the workflow instructions:\nthe ""*-handling"" reaction for every selection and harness return

== Workflow selection (no harness call) ==
Orch -> Orch : per ""workflow-selection-handling"" instruction —\nmatch the user's intent to one facilitated workflow
alt the intent maps to one workflow (the orchestrator's selection skill)
  Orch --> User : proposes it
else ambiguous or unmatched intent (optional engagement turns)
  Orch --> User : engages — answers, asks which workflow to enter
  User -> Orch : clarifies the intent
end
User -> Orch : assent — start the workflow\n(or continue an unfinished one — the harness\nresumes its latest open instance)

loop until ""3 resolve-step"" resolves no-next-step

== Step resolution ==
note over Host, Adapter
  H4 (""preToolUse"" — harness-command class) is a HOOK-EXECUTED
  boundary: the adapter runs ""3 resolve-step"" /
  ""4 resolve-step-model"" itself, attributed from its own event
  payload and bookkeeping (like every other hook invocation),
  and answers with a deny whose reason IS the report — the host
  relays it as the tool result, so the agent's command never runs
  and is never edited. The harness's own backstop (below) still
  rejects a sessionId that is not currently open and registered.
end note
Orch -> Host : mediated invocation — tool call:\n""harness.py resolve-step --workflow-slug <slug>""\n— plain line, no session id
Host -> Adapter : hook ""preToolUse"" — harness-command class
Adapter -> Adapter : deny if not one plain resolve-step / resolve-step-model\nrequest or if it carries session attribution; else\nresolve the current session via ""SessionTracker""
Adapter -> Harness : ""3 resolve-step""(sessionId: resolved, parentSessionId: null, workflowSlug)
Harness -> Harness : deduce the instance — continue the latest open one,\nor mint a new instance id (the opening is this very\nlog entry — no dedicated file, no id returned)
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: step-resolution,\nstep: { slug, actor, skills, instructions, artifact,\nconditions, capabilities } }\n(context.workflowInstanceId minted or continued)
Adapter --> Host : permissionDecision: deny +\nreason "SAFe agentic harness RESULT (resolve-step)" + report\n(the reason says: act on it, do not re-issue)
Host --> Orch : tool result — the step resolution\n(the terminal never ran the line)
Orch -> Host : mediated invocation — tool call:\n""harness.py resolve-step-model --workflow-slug <slug>""
Host -> Adapter : hook ""preToolUse"" — harness-command class
Adapter -> Harness : ""4 resolve-step-model""(sessionId: resolved, parentSessionId: null)
Harness -> Harness : deduce the session's in-flight step;\ncapabilities × catalog → model profile
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: resolved,\nprofile: { slug, score, costRank, reason } }
Adapter --> Host : permissionDecision: deny +\nreason "SAFe agentic harness RESULT (resolve-step-model)" + report
Host --> Orch : tool result — the model profile
Orch -> Orch : per ""step-resolution-handling"" instruction —\nrelay the resolution + profile verbatim

== Step dispatch (1 step instance = 1 agent = 1 session = 1 artifact instance) ==
Orch -> Host : ""task"" (the resolution verbatim:\nactor, model profile, skills, instructions)
Host -> Adapter : hook ""preToolUse"" — dispatch class
Adapter -> Harness : ""5 check-step-preconditions""(sessionId, parentSessionId: null)
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: pass | fail,\nconditionChecks: [{ condition, outcome, failureMessage? }, …] }
alt preconditions hold
  Adapter --> Host : pass (empty: the adapter never emits allow)
else a precondition fails
  Adapter --> Host : permissionDecision: deny +\npermissionDecisionReason (conditionChecks[] serialized)
  Host --> Orch : dispatch blocked, reports returned
  Orch -> Orch : per ""reports-handling"" instruction — produce the missing\nstate (via a prior step or the user), dispatch again
end
Host -> Adapter : hook ""subagentStart""
alt agentType correlates to an unresolved step-resolution entry
  Adapter -> Harness : ""0 start-session""(agent: agentType, sessionId,\nparentSessionId: the dispatching session)
  Harness -> Harness : correlates to the parent's latest unresolved\nstep-resolution entry for agentType
  Harness -> Harness : the step instance exists: create its step ref\n""refs/harness/steps/<workflowInstanceId>/<stepSlug>/<workerSessionId>""\n(from the previous step instance's tip when the base is\nunchanged, else the workspace branch tip) — no checkout:\nthe working tree stays on the workspace branch
  Harness --> Adapter : { session: { agent, sessionId, parentSessionId } }
  Adapter -> Harness : ""6 resolve-step-instructions""(sessionId, parentSessionId)
  Harness --> Adapter : { instructions: [the step's declared refs] }
  Adapter -> Harness : ""7 resolve-step-skills""(sessionId, parentSessionId)
  Harness --> Adapter : { skills: [the step's declared skill ids] }
  Adapter -> Adapter : render ""additionalContext"" —\ninline step refs + skill load directives
  Adapter --> Host : ""additionalContext"" = hint + step context
  Host --> Sub : session carries the step's constraints
else foreign subagent — no correlation
  Adapter --> Host : pass through — untouched, unlogged (C7)
end

== Step work — every write guarded ==
Sub -> Host : write artifact (host write tool)
Host -> Adapter : hook ""preToolUse"" — write class
Adapter -> Harness : ""8 check-step-authorization""(sessionId, parentSessionId,\nartifactPath, action)
Harness -> Harness : claim the artifact lock ""refs/harness/locks/<artifactPath>""\n(create-only; held by this step instance, or re-pointed from the\nstep instance a retry continues; held by another: deny)
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: allowed | denied,\nauthorization: { actor, artifactPath, action, resource, failureMessage? } }
alt privilege granted
  Adapter --> Host : pass (empty: the adapter never emits allow)\n(step instance in flight; artifact lock held;\nan unclaimed path was clean against HEAD)
  Host -> Host : execute the write — lands in the working tree\n(the staging area, not yet workspace state)
else no grant, no step instance in flight, or lock held by another
  Adapter --> Host : permissionDecision: deny (missing privilege / no step instance in flight /\nlock held by another step instance)
  Host --> Sub : write blocked, report returned
  Sub -> Sub : per its step instructions — proceed without the write,\nor return it to the orchestrator (privileged-author route)
end
Host -> Adapter : hook ""postToolUse"" — write class
Adapter -> Harness : ""9 check-step-artifact""(sessionId, parentSessionId, artifactPaths)
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: valid | reverted,\nartifactChecks?: [{ artifactPath, failureMessage, revert: { action, from } }, …] }
alt write is schema-valid
  Harness -> Harness : commit the validated bytes onto the step ref\n(temporary index; HEAD and working tree unmoved),\nattributed to the session — workspace state\ndoes not advance (only promotion does)
  Adapter --> Host : pass (empty)
else invalid write
  Harness -> Harness : discard the staged write — restore from the step\nref tip or HEAD / delete new: no commit ever held the invalid\nbytes (C6 — transactional by construction)
  Adapter --> Host : ""modifiedResult"" (write rejected: …) +\n""additionalContext"" (the retry instruction)
  Host --> Sub : failure message returned
  Sub -> Sub : per its step instructions — rewrite per the\nfailure message and retry the write
end

== Step close ==
Sub --> Host : worker session ends
Host -> Adapter : hook ""subagentStop""
Adapter -> Harness : ""11 end-session""(sessionId: agentId, no parentSessionId needed)
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: ended }\n(never surfaced to the host)
Adapter -> Adapter : ""SessionTracker"" deletes the worker session's record
Host -> Adapter : hook ""postToolUse"" — dispatch class
Adapter -> Harness : ""10 check-step-postconditions""(sessionId, parentSessionId: null)
Harness -> Harness : rebase the step ref onto the workspace branch in memory\n(merge-tree) if it moved (conflict: state-error\nstep-rebase-conflict); evaluate\ndelivery (whole step state + own commits) + postconditions\non the step state
alt step instance passes
  Harness -> Harness : promote — ONE atomic fast-forward of the workspace\nbranch ref to the step ref (compare-and-swap): the\nacceptance point; then sync the promoted paths' index\nentries, locks released; step ref kept\n(branch moved meanwhile: state-error step-rebase-conflict)
else step instance fails
  Harness -> Harness : withhold — no promotion or lock act: workspace branch and locks\nuntouched, step ref kept: a retry inherits both
end
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: pass | fail,\nconditionChecks: [{ condition, outcome, failureMessage? }, …],\npromotion: { outcome: promoted | withheld, workspaceCommit } }
alt postconditions hold — step journaled executed
  Adapter --> Host : pass (empty)
  Host --> Orch : dispatch returns — next iteration resolves the next step
else postconditions fail — step not journaled executed
  Adapter --> Host : ""additionalContext"" (failing conditions +\nthe re-resolve directive)
  Host --> Orch : dispatch returns with reports
  Orch -> Orch : per ""reports-handling"" instruction — retry inside the workflow,\ninvisible to the user: the next iteration re-resolves the failed step\n(the harness governs the sequencing, not the agent)
end

end

== Workflow return ==
Orch -> Host : mediated invocation — tool call:\n""harness.py resolve-step --workflow-slug <slug>""
Host -> Adapter : hook ""preToolUse"" — harness-command class
Adapter -> Harness : ""3 resolve-step""(sessionId: resolved, parentSessionId: null, workflowSlug)
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: no-next-step }\n(a reversible observation — never "done")
Adapter --> Host : permissionDecision: deny +\nreason "SAFe agentic harness RESULT (resolve-step)" + report
Host --> Orch : tool result — no-next-step
Orch -> Orch : per ""no-next-step-handling"" instruction\n(it names the advisory successors)
Orch --> User : end-to-end workflow results (delivered artifacts)\n+ options: reiterate the workflow / take a successor
note right of Orch
  The user sees workflow results only —
  never intermediate step results.
  Step retries happen inside the workflow:
  re-resolution on negative reports (invariant 7).
end note

== Turn close (""agentStop"" fires when the orchestrator returns to the user) ==
Host -> Adapter : hook ""agentStop""
Adapter -> Adapter : resolve the ending orchestrator session\nvia ""SessionTracker"" — never the raw conversation id\n(a never-registered session is a silent pass-through)
Adapter -> Harness : ""11 end-session""(sessionId)
Harness --> Adapter : { outcome: ended }\n(never surfaced to the host; no function runs\nfor a session whose end is never observed)
Adapter -> Adapter : ""SessionTracker"" deletes the session's record —\na later firing under a non-framework agent finds none:\nC7 pass-through, never a stale session

note right of Harness
  Configuration and workspace validity are
  internal enforcement, not functions:
  fail-fast configuration load at every
  instantiation; the workspace sweep as
  store capability behind CI's C6 gate
  (spec — Internal validation).
end note

@enduml
